,-0.0325605,-0.00475162,0.03291711,0.1960018,0.01228728,0.01291858,0.02717384,-0.001001,-0.01086643,0.11535866,0.04221653,-0.00708551,-0.04229762,0.11999649,0.05351868,-0.03383989,0.05606257,-0.0428836,0.01229775,0.02470051,-0.01139997,0.02030001,0.00803507,0.02388992,0.00421681,0.0867837,-0.01934762,0.01485896,-0.07128432,-0.04032524,-0.03807618,-0.00901455,-0.00296751,0.01310869,-0.00137925,-0.00626148,0.10661575,-0.01428609,-0.02488349,-0.06353141,-0.05414017,0.00091449,-0.02566518,0.08929905,0.05198544,0.04274401],"last_embed":{"hash":"uqru7a","tokens":449}}},"last_read":{"hash":"uqru7a","at":1762678884966},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1762678760063,"size":19483,"at":1762678872010,"hash":"uqru7a"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,16],"#":[17,426],"#**Purpose/Why**:":[427,442],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{1}":[429,433],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{2}":[434,434],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{3}":[435,435],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{4}":[436,436],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{5}":[437,438],"#**Purpose/Why**:#{6}":[439,442],"#**Core Explanation:**":[443,447],"#**Core Explanation:**#{1}":[445,447],"#FF5582A6;\">Think of them as a generalized way to \"point to\" and move through data. </mark>For example, if you have a vector `{10, 20, 30}`, an iterator can point to the first element (10), then be incremented to point to the second (20), and so on. Different types exist: input iterators (read-once), output iterators (write-once), forward iterators (move forward), bidirectional iterators (move forward/backward), and random access iterators (jump to any position).":[448,451],"#FF5582A6;\">Think of them as a generalized way to \"point to\" and move through data. </mark>For example, if you have a vector `{10, 20, 30}`, an iterator can point to the first element (10), then be incremented to point to the second (20), and so on. Different types exist: input iterators (read-once), output iterators (write-once), forward iterators (move forward), bidirectional iterators (move forward/backward), and random access iterators (jump to any position).#{1}":[450,451],"#**Related Concepts:**":[452,458],"#**Related Concepts:**#{1}":[454,454],"#**Related Concepts:**#{2}":[455,455],"#**Related Concepts:**#{3}":[456,456],"#**Related Concepts:**#{4}":[457,458],"#FFF3A3A6;\">Iterators can be thought of as a generalization of pointers</mark>. Raw pointers are a simple form of random access iterators for C-style arrays. However, iterators offer a more abstract and type-safe way to navigate various data structures, encapsulating the underlying access logic. Unlike raw pointers, iterators often carry information about the container they belong to, enabling bounds checking or other safety features (though not universally guaranteed).":[459,461],"#FFF3A3A6;\">Iterators can be thought of as a generalization of pointers</mark>. Raw pointers are a simple form of random access iterators for C-style arrays. However, iterators offer a more abstract and type-safe way to navigate various data structures, encapsulating the underlying access logic. Unlike raw pointers, iterators often carry information about the container they belong to, enabling bounds checking or other safety features (though not universally guaranteed).#{1}":[460,461],"#**Examples:**":[462,555],"#**Examples:**#{1}":[464,555],"#**Flashcards:**":[556,563],"#**Flashcards:**#{1}":[558,563]},"outlinks":[{"title":"STL Containers (vector, list, map, etc.)","target":"STL Containers (vector, list, map, etc.)","line":432},{"title":"C++ Smart Pointers","target":"C++ Smart Pointers","line":446},{"title":"STL Containers (vector, list, map, etc.)","target":"STL Containers (vector, list, map, etc.)","line":455},{"title":"Ranges (C++20)","target":"Ranges (C++20)","line":460}],"metadata":{"memory":"to_finish","tags":["#learned"],"language":["C++"],"review-date":null,"last-reviewed":"2025-08-23","scheda":"done","visit-count":5,"confidence-level":2,"consecutive-correct":2,"last-struggle-date":"2025-07-27","cssclasses":null},"last_embed":{"hash":"uqru7a","at":1762678884929},"key":"Computer Science/C++/C++ Iterators.md","task_lines":[]},
